    "result_text": "The full suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS). AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and both its tests are green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `contactPreference` = `EMAIL` when an email is present, otherwise `PHONE`, as a derived read-only field on the owner response.\n\nChanges, each in the place it belongs:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added `hasEmail()`, extracting the \"non-blank email\" check that was previously inlined.\n\n2. **`model/MembershipLevel.java`** \u2014 refactored to reuse `owner.hasEmail()` instead of duplicating the check.\n\n3. **`model/ContactPreference.java`** (new) \u2014 a small enum `EMAIL`/`PHONE` with `of(Owner)` holding the single derivation rule.\n\n4. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `contactPreference` mapping expression alongside the other derived fields (`locality`, `initials`, \u2026), delegating to `ContactPreference.of(owner).name()`.\n\n5. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema so the generated DTO carries the field, consistent with the sibling `locality` field.\n\nThe logic lives in one focused enum, the presence check is shared via `Owner.hasEmail()`, and the mapper follows the existing derived-field pattern \u2014 nothing became a catch-all.",
